# cela2027 — Git attributes
#
# Goals
#   1. One line-ending policy for every platform: LF in the repository AND in
#      every working tree (Windows included). No CRLF drift in reviews.
#   2. E2E fixtures are byte-exact evidence: Git must never normalise, merge,
#      or otherwise rewrite them. Their bytes are pinned in
#      e2e/fixtures/SHA256SUMS and verified by `node e2e/scripts/check-fixtures.mjs`.
#   3. Real binaries are declared explicitly instead of relying on heuristics.
#
# Policy details: docs/E2E_FIXTURES.md

# ── 1. Default: auto-detect text, always LF ───────────────────────────────
*                     text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text types (never let a misdetection turn these into binaries)
*.md                  text eol=lf
*.txt                 text eol=lf
*.json                text eol=lf
*.ndjson              text eol=lf
*.yml                 text eol=lf
*.yaml                text eol=lf
*.ts                  text eol=lf
*.tsx                 text eol=lf
*.js                  text eol=lf
*.mjs                 text eol=lf
*.cjs                 text eol=lf
*.css                 text eol=lf
*.py                  text eol=lf
*.sh                  text eol=lf
*.sql                 text eol=lf
.gitattributes        text eol=lf
.gitignore            text eol=lf
.env.example          text eol=lf
LICENSE               text eol=lf

# Lockfiles: text (kept diff-able so change guards can classify them)
package-lock.json     text eol=lf linguist-generated=true

# ── 2. E2E fixtures: byte-exact, never normalised ─────────────────────────
# -text  → no EOL conversion in either direction (working tree == blob)
# diff   → still human-reviewable for text-like fixtures
e2e/fixtures/**                 -text diff
e2e/fixtures/**/*.bin           binary
e2e/fixtures/**/*.png           binary
e2e/fixtures/**/*.zip           binary
# The manifest is regenerated, never hand-merged
e2e/fixtures/SHA256SUMS         -text diff -merge

# ── 3. Binary assets anywhere in the repository ───────────────────────────
*.png                 binary
*.jpg                 binary
*.jpeg                binary
*.gif                 binary
*.webp                binary
*.ico                 binary
*.pdf                 binary
*.woff                binary
*.woff2               binary
*.ttf                 binary
*.wasm                binary
*.zip                 binary
*.gz                  binary
